Calculating base stat totals
Summing base_stat for each pokemon_id gives its BST, which we then join with the species table to get an appropriate mapping. Legendary and mythical Pokemon are removed, because the number of legendaries varies a lot between generations and would skew the averages and we saw in the previous post that they have a much higher BST on average. The main intent here is to compare analyze power creep for regular Pokemon.

bst &lt;- pokemon_stats |&gt;
  group_by(pokemon_id) |&gt;
  summarize(bst = sum(base_stat))

regular &lt;- species |&gt;
  left_join(bst, by = c("id" = "pokemon_id")) |&gt;
  filter(is_legendary == 0, is_mythical == 0) |&gt;
  select(identifier, generation_id, bst)

head(regular)

